# Agent-rule files written by scripts/agent-rules/generate.mjs. Its --check
# mode (run by tests/test_agent_rules_drift.py) compares bytes, so a CRLF
# working tree (core.autocrlf=true, the Windows default) reads every one of
# them as stale. Pinning LF keeps a Windows checkout byte-identical to what the
# generator writes; normalising inside --check would instead accept a CRLF file
# that a later byte-level consumer might not (issue #278). Keep this list in
# step with the emit()/emitBlock() calls in generate.mjs.
AGENTS.md                               text eol=lf
.cursorrules                            text eol=lf
.windsurfrules                          text eol=lf
.clinerules                             text eol=lf
.cursor/rules/*.mdc                     text eol=lf
.github/copilot-instructions.md         text eol=lf
.github/instructions/*.instructions.md  text eol=lf
.windsurf/rules/*.md                    text eol=lf
.roo/rules/resolve-mcp.md               text eol=lf
.continue/rules/resolve-mcp.md          text eol=lf
